  "content": {
    "id": "v2-9cfdc-p26-practice-slot-3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Use concavity to decide whether the trapezoidal rule overestimates or underestimates $\\displaystyle\\int_1^3 x^3\\,dx$. Give a reason.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Overestimates: $f''(x)=6x>0$ on $[1,3]$, so the curve is concave up and the chords lie above it.",
      "worked": "Let $f(x)=x^3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=3x^2\\\\f''(x)&=6x\\end{align*}$$\nOn $1\\le x\\le3$, $f''(x)>0$, so the curve is concave up. The chords forming the tops of the trapezia lie above the curve, so the trapezoidal rule overestimates the integral.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
